hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2718","\nNarrated to us Isma'il ibn Musa al-Fazari, who said: Malik informed us.\nAnd narrated to us Ali ibn Khashram, who said: 'Abdullah ibn Wahb informed us, from Malik ibn Anas, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed Ramal (a brisk walk with quick, short steps, moving the shoulders) from the Black Stone to the Black Stone. 'Ali added: three times, and walked normally four times."
